{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Real-Time State Synchronization.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Real-Time State Synchronization.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"real time state synchronization real time state synchronization","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Real-Time State Synchronization.md","fileName":"Real-Time State Synchronization.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Real-Time State Synchronization","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 20:52\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Real-Time Web Communication]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Real-Time Web Communication","aspnetcore3andreact.pdf","gameprogrammingalgorithmsandtechniques.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Real-Time State Synchronization.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Real-Time State Synchronization.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"real time state synchronization real time state synchronization","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Real-Time State Synchronization.md","fileName":"Real-Time State Synchronization.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Real-Time State Synchronization","heading":"Real-Time State Synchronization","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Real-time state synchronization maps a received server event into the client state that drives the interface. A SignalR handler can append or replace the relevant value so React rerenders without a manual refresh.\n\nThe event payload and state transition must agree on identity and ordering. The live message improves freshness, while a later authoritative fetch can restore consistency after a missed or interrupted connection.\n\nIn a networked game, synchronization also depends on topology. A client-server model distributes authoritative updates from one server, while peer-to-peer simulations may exchange commands and require each machine to advance deterministic state in the same order.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Real-Time Web Communication","aspnetcore3andreact.pdf","gameprogrammingalgorithmsandtechniques.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Real-Time State Synchronization.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Real-Time State Synchronization.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"real time state synchronization real time state synchronization","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Real-Time State Synchronization.md","fileName":"Real-Time State Synchronization.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Real-Time State Synchronization","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[aspnetcore3andreact.pdf]]\n[[gameprogrammingalgorithmsandtechniques.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Real-Time Web Communication","aspnetcore3andreact.pdf","gameprogrammingalgorithmsandtechniques.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}